  "sourceTitle": "Welsh Rarebit",
  "sourceText": "Welsh Rarebit\nBy: Sheri Wetherell\nPublished: Friday, December 4, 2009 - 11:37pm\n\nIngredients\n\n\n\n\n4 tablespoons butter\n2 teaspoons Worcestershire sauce\n1 teaspoon salt\n1 teaspoon paprika\n1/2 teaspoon prepared mustard\n1 pound sharp Cheddar cheese, grated\n1 cup Beer\n2 eggs, slightly beaten\n1 tablespoon corn starch\n\nPreparation\n\n1 Melt butter, seasonings and cheese in a double boiler until cheese is soft.  2 Add corn starch to beer and slowly add eggs to mixture. Cook until thick. Serve very hot on toast.",
  "parsedSource": {
    "ingredients": [
      {
        "sourceText": "4 tablespoons butter"
      },
      {
        "sourceText": "2 teaspoons Worcestershire sauce"
      },
      {
